      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T13:46:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`first_glyph` is pointing to the first glyph code of the array of `hb_glyph_info_t`  of an `hb_buffer_t`, but the members of `hb_glyph_info_t` are other parts, not glyphs. I think this generally does not fit or squeeze well into an `SkSpan\u003cuint32_t\u003e` as the `Span` bounds checking expects contiguous memory regions. So we would have to massage the size of the SkSpan to artificially be as large as the array of `hb_glyph_info_t`, which is not really accurate. The API would look more like `Span`\u0027s but practically isn\u0027t, IMO, and would require cheats on the caller side.",
      "parentUuid": "3c35b119_9c5f517f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 49
